the redirect that will fail. If you are

00:16:53.660 --> 00:16:57.440
able to handle, see and handle that
redirect, then it will be fine.

00:16:57.440 --> 00:17:00.590
Right now there are no redirects
happening so you can submit

00:17:00.590 --> 00:17:03.950
HTTP request to the eutils and blast
and they'll function normally.

00:17:04.730 --> 00:17:09.650
They'll just come back to you as standard
status 200s, but once September 30

00:17:09.650 --> 00:17:14.000
happens, that will no longer be the
case, you'll be redirected. And so to

00:17:14.000 --> 00:17:18.500
simulate that redirect, point something
towards those test servers and you'll

00:17:18.500 --> 00:17:22.610
get the same 301 redirect that
will happen after September 30.

